			"notes": "## Unlimited Peripheral Works 1.9.0 for Minecraft 1.21.1\n\nAvailable for Fabric and NeoForge. The artifact named `peripheralworks-forge-1.21.1-1.9.0.jar` is the **NeoForge** build.\n\n### Added\n\n- Dedicated AE2 ME network peripheral and CC:Tweaked wired-network P2P tunnel.\n- AE2 cable-part and pattern-provider peripherals with configurable device APIs.\n- Linked AE2 wireless terminals and crafting terminals as turtle and pocket computer upgrades.\n- Crafting-job lifecycle APIs and AE2 storage-change subscriptions.\n- Shared `ae2_network_access` peripheral type and TypeScript provider for dedicated and wireless network access.\n- Pattern pedestal for encoding and inspecting crafting, processing, stonecutting and smithing patterns.\n\n### Changed and fixed\n\n- Ported the 1.20 branch's features to native Minecraft 1.21.1 data components, recipe APIs and NeoForge capabilities.\n- Centralized integration configuration with protection against reads before configuration is loaded.\n- Preserved the legacy `ae2` API when wrapping existing AE2 network blocks; the dedicated peripheral adds an explicit channel-owning option.\n- Preserved exact item/fluid component variants in pattern definitions, including validation and inventory-safety checks.\n- Corrected generated netherite peripheralium hub upgrade types.\n\n### Compatibility\n\n- Requires Minecraft 1.21.1 and Java 21.\n- AE2 integration is **NeoForge-only**, matching the existing 1.21 support matrix. The Fabric jar includes the supported shared/base functionality, not AE2 integration.\n- On 1.21, the pattern API's `snbt` field represents a data-component patch rather than legacy resource NBT; for example, `{\"minecraft:custom_data\":{custom:\"value\"}}`.\n\n### Verification\n\n- Full multi-loader build and TypeScript/Lua compilation passed.\n- Server GameTests: NeoForge 58/58; Fabric 32/32, in both minimal and full environments.\n- NeoForge without AE2: 33/33.\n- Client GameTests: NeoForge 5/5; Fabric 4/4, including pattern-pedestal rendering.\n- GitHub CI passed for the merged port: https://github.com/SirEdvin/UnlimitedPeripheralWorks/actions/runs/34531954424\n\nPort PR: https://github.com/SirEdvin/UnlimitedPeripheralWorks/pull/102\n\n### Re-release: optional AE2 resource fix\n\n- Replaced the 1.9.0 JARs with the merged fix that keeps AE2-only loot resources out of the base data pack when AE2 is absent.\n- Existing version and asset names are unchanged; download hashes have changed. Re-download the JARs and refresh any pinned hashes.\n- Source: `bfc8ec580f117760334424452194bb744c273076` (https://github.com/SirEdvin/UnlimitedPeripheralWorks/pull/104)."
		},
